  "body": "> Replaces #411, which GitHub closed when a review fix was pushed after the fork left NeoTech's network. This branch is #411's plus that fix.\n\n**Review fix (from #411's review):** the machine check now runs only where material crosses: in `carry_turn` for a carry, and in `walk`'s Clip arm. A later setup that takes its own new block on another machine is judged, not refused. Pinned by `setup_carry::a_new_block_on_another_machine_is_judged_not_refused`; setup_carry passes 9/9 and clippy is clean.\n\n## What changed\nFollow-up from the review of #401 (carry the machined body into the next setup).\n\n**The missing refusal.** #401's notes credit the cross-machine refusal to \"#390's refusal\", but no such check existed in the program sim. #390 is the browser tree. The only mount refusals (#343) sit at generation and at post, and the sim walk checked only the **active** setup's machine kind.\n\nChanges in `crates/app/src/stock_sim_carry.rs` (the constant is re-exported from `stock_sim.rs`):\n- **New refusal:** `CARRY_MACHINE_REFUSAL`, raised by `one_machine(world, from, to)`. It compares the two setups' own machines (`setup_mount::machine_of`: the setup's machine, else the document's). The message names both setups and both machines, e.g. `'Setup1' on no machine, 'Setup2' on Tormach 770M`.\n- **At the carry:** `carry::entry` refuses a carry onto another machine. The lathe/mill-turn check now reads the two setups' shared machine instead of the active setup's. Because `entry` is shared with the rest reading (#318), an op in the later setup is refused at generation with `REST_CARRY_REFUSAL` plus the machine reason.\n- **In the program walk:** `carry::walk` (behind `simulate_document` and `incoming_body`) refuses every setup change onto another machine. That includes a clip between setups that hold the part the same way, because a clip keeps what the earlier setup left standing.\n- **Clip in the rest reading:** deliberately **not** refused. There, the later setup starts from its own block and reads nothing across. Refusing it would block generation in every two-machine document whose setups hold the part alike, which #343 allows.\n\n**Off-grid alignment** is represented exactly, so it is pinned rather than refused. `Body::carry` takes the image origin from the turned lattice corners, so every image cell centre is a transformed source centre, and nothing snaps to the old grid.\n\n`docs/decisions/317-carry-body.md` is left unedited, per the decisions README (a PR does not edit another PR's file). `docs/decisions/404-carry-machine-check.md` records the correction.\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `sim/tests/stock_carry.rs::an_odd_lattice_carried_off_the_grid_keeps_whole_cells`: a 7 × 5 lattice at 0.5 mm with a distinct height per column. It is carried through a flip over X and a quarter turn, each translated by (0.37, −1.13). The test checks a one-to-one column map, image centres equal to the transformed source centres, exact heights, and exact origin, volume and bounds.\n- `app/tests/setup_carry.rs::a_carry_between_setups_on_different_machines_is_refused_by_name`: generation is refused naming both setups and both machines. `simulate_document` and `incoming_body` error, and undo restores the carry bit for bit.\n- `app/tests/setup_carry.rs::a_clip_between_setups_on_different_machines_is_refused_by_name`: generation still works, and the program sim refuses by name.\n- `app/tests/setup_carry.rs::a_flip_about_a_centre_off_the_grid_carries_whole_cells`: a part centred off-grid in a 61 × 47 block, flipped. The incoming body is the exact mirror, and the verdict shows no gouge.\n\n## Readings\n- These suites all pass: `setup_carry` 8, `rest_across_setups` 5, `stock_sim_document` 9, `setup_align` 9, `setup_mount` 6, `setup_relative` 8, `setups` 11, app lib 95, `stock_carry` 7, `stock_sim` 24.\n- **Quick gate:** post, sim and app are green. The remaining reds also fail on main: `swarf_pose_continuity` (#351) and the GPU headless tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n- No posted G-code and no GUI change.\n\nChangelog: The program sim refuses by name to carry or clip the stock between setups on different machines (it used to check only the active setup's machine) (#404)\n\nFixes #404\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
